.Dd July 3, 2026
.Dt BPM 1
.Os Blueberry Linux
.Sh NAME
.Nm bpm
.Nd Blueberry package manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the package manager for Blueberry Linux. It installs
.Pa .bpm
packages from HTTP(S) mirrors. The repository index is ed25519-signed and lists
a SHA-256 for every package, and both are checked before anything touches the
disk. Downloads stay in a local cache, so you can reinstall, roll back or
downgrade without a network.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm install Ar name|file ...
Install packages and whatever they depend on. You can also pass a local
.Pa .bpm
or
.Pa .pkg.tar.zst
file directly.
.It Cm remove Ar name ...
Remove packages. If something else still needs one, bpm refuses unless you pass
.Fl f .
.It Cm autoremove
Remove dependencies nothing needs anymore. Without
.Fl y
it only lists them.
.It Cm update
Fetch the signed
.Pa bpm.index
from each repository and verify it. An index older than the last one accepted is
rejected, so a stale mirror can't roll you back.
.It Cm upgrade
Upgrade every installed package that has a newer version in the index. On a
btrfs root with
.Nm blueberry-snapshot
installed, a snapshot is taken first.
.It Cm outdated
List packages with a newer version available, one per line as
.Ql name<TAB>installed<TAB>available .
Changes nothing.
.It Cm audit
Report known CVEs in the installed packages. Mapped packages are checked against
NVD (C and system software) or OSV (Go and Rust bits), and anything without a
mapping is listed as untracked. Extra arguments go to the audit engine, e.g.
.Fl Fl json
or
.Fl Fl fail-on Cm high
(exit non-zero if anything at that severity or worse turns up). Set
.Ev NVD_API_KEY
to get past NVD's anonymous rate limit.
.It Cm rollback Ar name
Go back to the newest cached version older than the installed one.
.It Cm downgrade Ar name Ns Op = Ns Ar version
Install a specific cached version, or the previous one if no
.Ar version
is given.
.It Cm search Ar term
Search the repository index by name and description.
.It Cm list
List installed packages and their versions.
.It Cm info Ar name
Show a package's metadata, from the local database if installed, otherwise from
the index.
.It Cm why Ar name
Show which installed packages need this one, and whether you installed it
yourself.
.It Cm depends Ar name
Print a package's dependency tree. Packages the base system provides are marked
.Ql (base) .
.It Cm files Ar name
List the files a package owns.
.It Cm clean Op Fl -all
Prune the download cache. The two newest versions of each package are kept so
.Cm rollback
and
.Cm downgrade
still have something to use;
.Fl -all
empties it completely.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Skip the disk space, file conflict and reverse dependency checks.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev BPM_ROOT
Install into the given directory instead of
.Pa / .
Scriptlets and
.Xr ldconfig 8
are run chrooted into that root.
.It Ev BPM_ALLOW_UNSIGNED
Accept an index with a missing or bad signature. For development only.
.It Ev BPM_NO_SCRIPTLETS
Skip pre/post-install scriptlets and service enablement.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/bpm/db
Installed-package database.
.It Pa /var/lib/bpm/cache
Downloaded packages, also used by rollback and downgrade.
.It Pa /var/lib/bpm/index
The synced repository index.
.It Pa /etc/bpm/repos.conf
Repositories and their mirrors.
.It Pa /etc/bpm/provided
Packages the base image already provides. Dependencies on them count as met.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr makewhatis 8
.Pp
After every transaction
.Nm
rebuilds the man page index, so new pages show up in
.Xr man 1
and
.Xr apropos 1 .
